*  g-cn2 -- the ERROR lane: an UNDECLARED &name read inside an
*  EVAL-compiled fragment.  The fragment never folds, so the read
*  reaches the cell, finds no binding, and raises 342 with the name.
*  RECORDED, NOT RULED: the manual (p.131) says EVAL FAILS when
*  evaluation of its argument fails, whereas SCRIP ABORTS here -- the
*  error-to-statement-failure mechanism is &ERRLIMIT, which SCRIP does
*  not have yet (rung KW-5, same gap kw_protected_write is parked on).
*  This witness pins TODAY'S behaviour in both media so KW-5 moves it
*  deliberately rather than silently.  .err_sno + no .ref is the repo
*  convention for an abort lane (streams checked separately: m4 buffers
*  stdout to exit, m3 does not, so 2>&1 interleaving is NOT comparable).
	&USER_DECLARED_CONSTANTS = 1
	&N = 42
	OUTPUT = 'before=' &N
	X = EVAL('&NEVERSET')
	OUTPUT = 'UNREACHED'
END
